Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: retain software ingress on mixed IPQ40xx flowtables

DESS and QCA WiFi share the LAN bridge but only EDMA can bind hardware
offload. Keep software hooks for devices reporting EOPNOTSUPP so both
directions remain accelerated in software when DESS rejects their route.
Other setup failures remain fatal. Apply the same policy on unbind.

Signed-off-by: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>

--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
@@ -1265,6 +1265,13 @@
 	else
 		err = nf_flow_table_indr_offload_cmd(&bo, flowtable, dev, cmd,
 						     &extack);
+	/* Hardware offload is opportunistic: keep the software ingress hook
+	 * on ports without an offload binding (for example QCA WiFi). The
+	 * hardware callbacks still reject unsupported routes, leaving those
+	 * flows in the software table. Propagate genuine setup failures.
+	 */
+	if (err == -EOPNOTSUPP)
+		return 0;
 	if (err < 0)
 		return err;
 
